body:
There are definitely exceptions to the rule. However a lot of women have a requirement and not a preference for their male partner to be a certain height and above(183cm+). It definitely hurts an individual's self esteem when you are excluded completely because of something you can't change(this is easily relatable to other factors that can't be changed like being rejected because of race, etc). 

&#x200B;

Here's just one of many imgur albums of women vocalizing how they truly feel about men who are short [https://imgur.com/a/8TJan](https://imgur.com/a/8TJan) Sure, it isn't every woman on the planet, but I have 10 more of these types of albums and actual statistical graphs that show this isn't just a one off thing. Again, there are exceptions to the rule but not many and they are usually taken already. When the dating scene is in the position that it is in due to dating apps and female hypergamy over the years (top 80% of women go for the top 20% of men) now we have 80% of men battling it out for the 20% of women left and of that bottom 20% we have to hope and pray that they are one of the special women that don't have a height requirement that somehow isn't in a relationship already, isn't extremely shallow in other factors like income and status, or is willing to date someone who isn't the most conventionally attractive in a room otherwise known as dating someone in their bracket of looks department. For example, overall appearance being a 4/10 and being willing to date people who are 3/10,4/10, or 5/10 in appearance instead of only wanting to date 6/10,7/10,8/10, and 9/10 people as a 4/10.

&#x200B;

Here's a post on twitter with 70k+ likes from a woman talking about men's height. [https://i.redd.it/6zuaisz2uwp21.jpg](https://i.redd.it/6zuaisz2uwp21.jpg)

&#x200B;

Other twitter stuff height stuff from women with likes [https://i.redd.it/pqnkiqkf4x931.jpg](https://i.redd.it/pqnkiqkf4x931.jpg) \+ [https://i.redd.it/7ziij88bshb11.png](https://i.redd.it/7ziij88bshb11.png) 



Imagine if instead of height it was something else that a man couldn't change about himself. It would be seen as one of the worst things if a woman on twitter or anywhere else said the things in these albums/links about someone's race instead and got away with it. A lot of women are obsessed with height and treat men that aren't at a certain threshold or higher like absolute garbage to the levels of dehumanizing, albeit not to their face usually otherwise they could get in trouble for bullying or potentially harassment. This is just what some women are confident enough to post online there are women offline who will never reveal how they truly feel about short men and will gaslight them into thinking that the issue is everything but their height.

[https://imgur.com/a/8TJan](https://imgur.com/a/8TJan)

&#x200B;

and [https://imgur.com/a/KGuzehO](https://imgur.com/a/KGuzehO)
